INT. ICE-DRILL RIG "CALLISTO ONE" - CONTROL CAGE - NIGHT

A steel box bolted to a frozen moon. Gauges flicker. A tiny window shows black sky and a bruised planet.

NASRIN, 38, mission engineer, holds a pressure valve with both hands. JOSEPH, 50, geologist, lies on the floor with a bleeding scalp and a laugh like a cough.

The radio SQUEALS.

NAKAMURA (V.O.)
(over radio)
Callisto One, Nakamura at Orbital. Report depth.

Nasrin thumbs the key.

NASRIN
Four kilometers. We hit something.

NAKAMURA (V.O.)
Define something.

NASRIN
It rang. Like a bell.

Joseph sits up. He grips her ankle, and she looks down.

JOSEPH
Don't pull the bit.

NASRIN
Pressure's spiking.

JOSEPH
Don't pull the bit.

She doesn't. The gauges climb. Alarms scream. Then, all at once, every needle drops to zero. Silence.

NAKAMURA (V.O.)
Callisto One, say again.

Nasrin looks at Joseph. He is staring at the floor, where a pale blue light is rising through the grating, and he is smiling.

NASRIN
(into radio)
Nakamura. We're through.
